# The line `int: x 5` writes what stands in its slot when it runs (the author 2026-11-11, R12; plan M11 5a, B5): the
# first launch of Self finds 5 there and adds 1, publishing 6; the second finds the published 6 and gives 7.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# Self is launched over itself in the code of main, which reads first and second after each launch; self_x is the x of
# Self at the end, which the dump of the root Structure Self used to show.
sub: main () (
    Self:
        int: x 5
        x := x + 1
    int: first 0
    int: second 0
)
    call: Self
    first := Self\x
    call: Self
    second := Self\x
main()
int: first main\data\first
int: second main\data\second
int: self_x main\data\Self\x
